    challengesLabel: THE CHALLENGES
    challenge: <p data-end="611" data-start="349"><strong data-end="389" data-start="349">Complex quotations and work packages</strong><br data-end="392" data-start="389"/>Every construction site is unique. Structuring a quotation with detailed work packages — items, materials, labor hours — takes too much time in Excel. And an error in one work package impacts the entire billing process.</p><p data-end="808" data-start="613"><strong data-end="656" data-start="613">Time tracking and profitability by site</strong><br data-end="659" data-start="656"/>Without a centralized tool, it is impossible to know whether a project is profitable before it is completed. Hours recorded on paper arrive too late.</p><p data-end="1003" data-start="810"><strong data-end="851" data-start="810">Planning and subcontractor management</strong><br data-end="854" data-start="851"/>Coordinating several subcontractors on the same site, planning interventions, and validating their invoices without losing track is a daily
      headache.</p><p data-end="1194" data-start="1005"><strong data-end="1040" data-start="1005">Periodic maintenance management</strong><br data-end="1043" data-start="1040"/>Managing recurring maintenance contracts, planning interventions, and generating the related invoices without spending administrative time every month.</p><p data-end="1416" data-start="1196"><strong data-end="1216" data-start="1196">Billing &amp; PEPPOL</strong><br data-end="1219" data-start="1216"/>Billing at the right time based on the actual progress of the site, collecting payments on site, and complying with the Belgian 2026 e-invoicing obligation — natively, not with a last-minute patch.</p>
